From 06b5d5788f8546402c603d5e1ef552f0c4221642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 01:28:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] F1 PGXP rows persist (settings.toml [pgxp]); Reset row last
 and forgets them

The Advanced rows used to be session-only: the PGXP mod's activation put
the shipped defaults back at every boot. Now any change is written to a
[pgxp] section of settings.toml and applied at boot after the mod's
activation, so it wins; every settings write (F1 save, launcher launch,
launcher quit) stamps the section back in. "Reset PGXP to GT2 defaults"
moves to the bottom of the section, restores the shipped values, and
drops the section so the title follows the mod again (actions do not
auto-save, so it saves explicitly).
---
